WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.110
On many world maps, Greenland appears
larger than all of South America.

2
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.350
This is the Mercator projection.

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.890
It is very useful in navigation.

4
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.610
Now spin a globe, and look
at the same two places again.

5
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.710
So which picture is right?

6
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.510
Is Greenland really bigger?

7
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.430
Or did mapmakers want
it to look important?

8
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.730
In this mission, you'll sort
maps by what they're for,

9
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:27.270
from road atlases to
choropleths and cartograms.

10
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.570
Then you'll compare different ways of
turning a round Earth into a flat map,

11
00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:34.330
and match each one to a job.

12
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:39.250
Your mission: explain why so many world
maps make Greenland look larger than South

13
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.120
America.
